-- Q12975: Prospective Analysis and Forecasting [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under regression analysis per ASC 275-10, a prediction interval for an individual observation is always wider than a confidence interval for the mean at the same X value. The prediction interval incorporates both sampling error in the estimated regression line and the inherent scatter of individual observations around the mean.
Wrong (A): The confidence interval for the mean is narrower, not wider, because it only estimates where the average response falls without accounting for individual variability.
Wrong (B): The two intervals are not identical; the prediction interval includes an additional variance component for individual observation scatter that the confidence interval excludes.
Wrong (D): The prediction interval is wider, not narrower, precisely because forecasting a single observation involves more uncertainty than estimating the mean response.$EXPL$
